  "explanation": "The question asks when the Howard County Courthouse was built. Multiple documents provide conflicting dates depending on the location and which courthouse is being referenced:\n\n- **1880**: Document D1S1 and D2S5 explicitly state that the Howard County Courthouse in Cresco, Iowa, was built in 1880.\n- **1906**: Document D4S2 refers to the third courthouse in Howard County, Iowa, which was begun in October 1905 and opened in 1906.\n- **1920**: Document D5S1 claims the Howard County Courthouse in Cresco, Iowa, was built in 1920 — this appears to be a conflicting or incorrect statement.\n- **1912**: Document D7S4 states that the Howard County Courthouse in St. Paul, Nebraska, was built in 1912.\n\nEach of these dates corresponds to a different Howard County Courthouse in different locations (Iowa, Nebraska), or possibly different iterations of the same courthouse. Since the question does not specify a location, all valid referents and their corresponding dates are preserved."
}
